# The Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore when deciding what to upload, so
# /public/work being gitignored is not enough — without this file the CLI ships
# the whole source render archive. That has two consequences, both bad:
#
#   1. The masters get served publicly at /work/<slug>/<file>. Verified: a
#      1.3MB PNG returned HTTP 200 from a deployment.
#   2. Every deploy uploads ~250MB instead of ~7MB.
#
# `npm run media` derives the WebP in public/media that the site actually
# serves. The masters stay on disk as the master copy and never ship.
public/work

# Excluded by the CLI's own defaults too, but named here because a
# .vercelignore replaces .gitignore rather than adding to it.
node_modules
.next
.git
.env*
